# Evidence artifacts are committed byte-for-byte (see sim/README.md and
# layout/README.md: records are append-only, and "append-only" is worth
# little if a checkout can silently rewrite the bytes). `-text` disables
# both end-of-line normalization on commit and conversion on checkout, so a
# raw ngspice/klt output stays exactly what the tool emitted -- ngspice on
# some platforms emits CRLF, and normalizing it would change the SHA-256 a
# record pins.
sim/smoke_test.ngspice.out -text
sim/**/corners/**/*.log -text
sim/**/mc-draws/**/*.log -text
layout/**/reports/**/*.gds binary
layout/**/reports/**/*.spice -text
sim/**/netlist-snapshots/**/*.spice -text

# BEGIN LOOM-MANAGED (merge drivers, #4528)
# install-metadata.json is a machine-local install stamp (loom_version,
# loom_commit, last_resync, loom_source) that every host's resync
# re-writes -- always keep our side on a merge conflict; the file is
# fully re-derived by the next resync regardless of which side "wins".
.loom/install-metadata.json merge=ours
# END LOOM-MANAGED (merge drivers, #4528)
